{
  \"contract\": \"board-build-plan/v1\",
  \"artifacts\": [
    {
      \"alias\": \"title\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_text\",
        \"text\": \"OCEAN CLEANUP PORTFOLIO  |  "'$2.0M DECISION BRIEF",
        "placement": {"target": {"kind": "auto"}}
      }
    },
    {
      "alias": "recommendation",
      "recipe": {
        "kind": "native_card",
        "title": "BOARD DECISION — RECOMMENDED MIX",
        "body": "APPROVE: $900k River Interception  |  $650k Ghost Gear  |  $450k Coastal Collection'"\\n\\nModeled 12-month outcome: ~1,610 tonnes managed (range 1,150–2,050). Blended modeled cost: ~"'$1,242/tonne. Portfolio execution risk: MODERATE.'"\\n\\nRelease 70% at signing and 30% after 90-day gates. This balances high-volume prevention, high-harm debris removal, and durable local delivery capacity.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"river\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"1  RIVER INTERCEPTION + HOTSPOT CAPTURE\",
        \"body\": \"ALLOCATION  "'$900k  •  45%'"\\nIMPACT  ~900 t/year prevented  •  range 650–1,150\\nCOST  ~"'$1,000/t  •  range ~$780–$1,385'"\\nRISK  MEDIUM\\n\\nBest at: stopping concentrated leakage before it reaches open water.\\nKey dependency: permits, flood-season uptime, verified end destination.\\n90-DAY GATE: 2 priority sites live; ≥150 t independently weighed; ≥80% uptime.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"gear\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"2  GHOST GEAR RECOVERY + PREVENTION\",
        \"body\": \"ALLOCATION  "'$650k  •  32.5%'"\\nIMPACT  ~260 t/year recovered or prevented  •  range 180–360\\nCOST  ~"'$2,500/t  •  range ~$1,805–$3,610'"\\nRISK  MEDIUM–HIGH\\n\\nBest at: removing entanglement hazards with outsized ecosystem harm per tonne.\\nKey dependency: safe retrieval, fisher participation, port disposal chain.\\n90-DAY GATE: ≥45 t recovered; ≥70% chain-of-custody; 2 prevention agreements.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"coastal\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"3  COASTAL COLLECTION + MARKET ACCESS\",
        \"body\": \"ALLOCATION  "'$450k  •  22.5%'"\\nIMPACT  ~450 t/year captured  •  range 320–540\\nCOST  ~"'$1,000/t  •  range ~$835–$1,405'"\\nRISK  MEDIUM–LOW\\n\\nBest at: repeatable local collection, sorting, and leakage prevention.\\nKey dependency: buyer demand, fair worker terms, contamination control.\\n90-DAY GATE: 4 community partners active; ≥75 t verified; ≥65% saleable recovery.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"rules\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"DECISION RULES — AGREE BEFORE FUNDING\",
        \"body\": \"1. FUND only with baseline, weighing method, chain-of-custody, and named owner.\\n2. RELEASE final 30% only if ≥80% of the 90-day impact gate is met and safety/permits are green.\\n3. REALLOCATE up to 15% after two missed monthly gates: move funds to the strongest verified performer.\\n4. PROTECT at least 20% for ghost gear unless safety or permits stop work; ecological harm is not captured by "'$/tonne alone.'"\\n5. STOP immediately for unsafe operations, unverifiable disposal, double-counting, or material local opposition.\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"week_one\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"FIRST WEEK — THREE ACTIONS\",
        \"body\": \"1  DAY 1  •  Ratify the mix, 70/30 tranches, 90-day gates, and one accountable portfolio owner.\\n\\n2  DAYS 2–3  •  Require a three-page evidence pack from each delivery partner: baseline, permits, operating plan, unit-cost quote, and end-destination proof.\\n\\n3  DAYS 4–5  •  Sign milestone agreements, commission independent measurement, and open a board dashboard with tonnes, "'$/tonne, uptime, safety, chain-of-custody, and community acceptance."
      }
    },
    {
      "alias": "debate",
      "recipe": {
        "kind": "native_card",
        "title": "BOARD DEBATE — FOUR QUESTIONS",
        "body": "• What are we optimizing: tonnes, ecosystem harm avoided, or durable local capacity?'"\\n• Is 32.5% for ghost gear enough to reflect its ecological leverage despite higher "'$/tonne?'"\\n• Who may exercise the 15% reallocation rule, and how quickly?\\n• Which downside matters most: seasonal under-delivery, unsafe retrieval, weak markets, or unverifiable disposal?\"
      }
    },
    {
      \"alias\": \"assumptions\",
      \"recipe\": {
        \"kind\": \"native_card\",
        \"title\": \"MODEL NOTES — MAKE ASSUMPTIONS VISIBLE\",
        \"body\": \"Working decision model, not an audited forecast. “Impact” means plastic prevented from entering the ocean or recovered with a verified end destination over 12 months; no double-counting across programs.\\n\\nRanges express delivery uncertainty, not statistical confidence. Budget figures include program delivery and measurement. Replace these modeled estimates with site-specific partner quotes and baselines during week one.\"
      }
    }
  ],
  \"connections\": [
    {\"kind\": \"visual\", \"label\": \"45%  •  "'$900k", "source": {"alias": "recommendation"}, "target": {"alias": "river"}},
    {"kind": "visual", "label": "32.5%  •  $650k", "source": {"alias": "recommendation"}, "target": {"alias": "gear"}},
    {"kind": "visual", "label": "22.5%  •  $450k", "source": {"alias": "recommendation"}, "target": {"alias": "coastal"}}
  ],
  "layout": {
    "kind": "grid",
    "anchor": {"alias": "title"},
    "members": ["recommendation", "river", "gear", "coastal", "rules", "week_one", "debate", "assumptions"],
    "columns": 3,
    "column_gap": 64,
    "row_gap": 56,
    "align": "start",
    "placement": {"clearance": 72, "preferred_directions": ["below"]}
  }
}
JSON'

